# The ScamShield seed-data shard files are append-only: two independent
# writers (this session's content routines and the scheduled
# generate-*.yml bots) each add new, self-contained entries to the end
# of the same files, on independent schedules. A plain merge sees that
# as a conflict even though the right resolution is always "keep both."
#
# git's built-in `union` driver used to do that job, and it is the wrong
# tool: union works line by line, and every entry is wrapped in the same
# boilerplate ("{" ... "}," or "X.push({" ... "});"). When both sides
# append, the diff matches that boilerplate as shared context and union
# emits ONE object literal containing BOTH bodies, every property
# duplicated. On 2026-09-17 that took delivery down with TS1117 ("An
# object literal cannot have multiple properties with the same name")
# across four scams shards, stranding 14 content commits.
#
# `scamseed` is scamshield-national/scripts/merge-seed-shard.js, which
# merges these files entry by entry instead of line by line, so it
# cannot interleave two entries, and refuses the merge (leaving an
# ordinary conflict) on anything it does not fully understand.
#
# The driver has to be configured to run. deliver-content-to-main.yml
# does that itself; for a local checkout run:
#   npm --prefix scamshield-national run install-merge-driver
# Without it git falls back to a plain text merge, which conflicts
# rather than corrupting, so an unconfigured checkout is safe.
scamshield-national/backend/src/db/seed-data/scams/*.ts merge=scamseed
scamshield-national/backend/src/db/seed-data/notorious/*.ts merge=scamseed
scamshield-national/backend/src/db/seed-data/guides/*.ts merge=scamseed
